    "created_at": "2022-03-28T05:51:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-28T05:51:10Z",
    "body": "> The key difference is that multiple opaque range responses are OK as long as they're from the same origin - they don't have to be the same URL.\r\n\r\nCan you elaborate on the reasons for this change in approach please?\r\n\r\nIf an attacker knows the content of some of the files from the origin being attacked, then it would seem plausible that they might be able to piece together leading bytes of their choice and so still succeed in the attacks that the URL check was intended to prevent.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1080220990/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
      "hooray": 0,
      "confused": 0,
